  "problem": "Hospital wide/tall CSV files could treat a metadata row as the variable schema. Wide and tall synthetic representations could lose payer/plan associations. Format equivalence could be treated as proof that two real hospital files describe identical periods/services. Partial or malformed rows could fabricate zero prices.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Hospital CSV parsing lives in packages/connectors/mrf/hospital-csv.mjs. CMS wide and tall CSV v3.0.0 official fictional examples are pinned. A generic CSV header parser cannot misclassify a metadata row as the variable schema. Wide and tall synthetic representations yield equivalent selected charges without losing payer/plan associations. Format equivalence applies to fixture values only and does not prove two real hospital files describe identical periods/services. Malformed rows remain visible and cannot fabricate zero prices. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
